+    en: { title: 'Best Earbuds with LDAC or aptX (Hi-Res Audio Codecs)', description: 'Wireless earbuds supporting LDAC or an aptX variant, the Bluetooth codecs capable of carrying more audio data than standard SBC/AAC for a genuine Hi-Res-eligible connection.', intro: 'Bluetooth audio quality depends heavily on which codec your phone and earbuds actually negotiate. LDAC and aptX (including aptX HD and aptX Adaptive) carry meaningfully more data than the SBC or AAC codec every pair of earbuds supports by default, but only when both your phone and your earbuds support the same one.', sections: [['Codec support alone is not enough', 'Your phone also needs to support the same codec — LDAC is common on Android, largely absent on iPhone, so check your phone before choosing earbuds for this reason alone.'], ['SBC and AAC are not automatically bad', 'AAC in particular performs well on iPhone. A higher-bitrate codec mainly matters if your source files and your listening environment can actually take advantage of the extra data.'], ['We record what is verified per model', 'Codec support is stored per model in our catalog rather than assumed from a brand or price tier — some inexpensive models do support LDAC, and some expensive ones do not.']] },
